(1) In this Part—
  dramatic work (戲劇作品) includes a work of dance or mime;
  literary work (文學作品) means any work, other than a dramatic or musical work, which is written, spoken or sung, and accordingly includes—
    (a) a compilation of data or other material, in any form, which by reason of the selection or arrangement of its contents constitutes an intellectual creation, including but not limiting to a table;
