(1) If, with respect to a contract for the sale of goods or supply of services in which one of the parties deals as consumer, the court finds the contract or any part of the contract to have been unconscionable in the circumstances relating to the contract at the time it was made, the court may—
  (a) refuse to enforce the contract;
  (b) enforce the remainder of the contract without the unconscionable part;
